A||||4||Shaun41178||3.4 making 245 hp, no sweat||||1||
Z||000000||Shaun41178||11-05-2001||03:35 AM||||I found this on the web.  can't believe I was able to get part numbers and everything too. Its about the 90 Beretta Pace Car<P>The specs on that actual Indy pace Car Beretta (the one used in the race,<BR>not the 7500 Beretta Indy's sold in 1990):<P>3.4 V6 245hp @ 6800rpm / 220lb-ft @ 4500rpm.<BR>It had an electronically controlled 4-speed auto tranny with a 3.43 gearset in the differential. Chevy reported times of 0-60 in 5.8 and the 1/4 in 13.8@105.<P>-Chevy aluminum engine block (pn 10051141) bored to 92mm<BR>-Extra-hard cast iron crankshaft (pn10078981); cross-drilled main bearings for added oiling<BR>-Melling oil pump (part number 10127575) with increased volume and pressure capacity; repositioned oil pump pickup tube<BR>-Windage tray added to minimize oil aeration<BR>-Erson solid tappet camshaft (pn F302F306  with 0.562 inch lift, 88 degrees overlap<BR>-Isky solid lifters (pn 202H)<BR>-Isky 110lb valve springs (pn 6005)<BR>-Crane roller rocker arms (pn 25752-12); modified for clearance to inlet manfold, valve covers and valve spring caps where required<BR>-Custom-made rocker studs by Ryan Falconer Enterprises<BR>-Modified production splayed valve cylinder heads with ported and polished intake and exhaust ports and unshrouded intake valve<BR>-Aluminum cast pistons fly-cut to provide 0.110 inch clearance<BR>-Modified production 3.1 liter manifold with existing intake runners<BR> replaced with 1.25 x 2.00 inch runners with 6.5 inch through-manifold ld runner length<BR>-Hand-built intake plenum similar to that used on the Corvette L98 engine<BR>-Production L98 Corvette throttle body weith heating system removed<BR>-Custom-made fuel rails of stainless steel tubing with Aeroquip fittings<BR>-High capacity fuel injectors from turbocharged 3.8 90-degree V6<BR>-Hand-made tubular tuned exhaust headers of 1.625 inch cold roll with wenty-four inch tubes and thirty-one inch collector.<P>Lets see I have the aluminum block.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Have a 3.1 crank, rods and pistons, have gen 3 heads which flow better then the gen 2 used on the beretta so minimal to no porting will be necessary to achieve same flow.  Stock 3100 oil pump should do.  Nice big camshaft.  I am sure one can find out more info about the cam by cross referencing that part number with Erson.  Same for valvesprings.  Darn thing tells you how to make the intake and exhaust manifolds.<P>What do you guys say?  Should I build something like this?  Take 70 pounds out of the back and perhaps more with the a/c out.  Throw the bottle on it?  shold be good for low 13's I would think.  Sounds like fun.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Smoooooth GT||11-05-2001||04:47 AM||||DO IT!!!!  let us know.. Steve||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wannabe||11-05-2001||09:41 AM||||Not to be a wet blanket but...I drooled over that build up for weeks before I realized that for the money it would take to do it, you could do just about any other type of swap, including N*, 3.8SC, LT1 etc etc. No doubt it would be a screamer if you have the funds to do it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lou_dias||11-05-2001||12:17 PM||||How big is the Corvette throttle body.<BR>I think we all know by now that are fieros are limited in getting air into the engine and that's where you'll see the biggest gains.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||11-05-2001||01:13 PM||||Low 13's on the bottle?<P>I would say off the bottle mid 13's. 12's on the juice easily.<P>Beretta's Don't launch too well  ,I can't imagine with 245hp on tap..Torque steer all over the place.<P>I believe the stock TB on an L98 is 52mm (mines in the back of the garage surroded by corvairs and Fiero , so I can't get to it)I have seen the L98 TB adapted to a Fiero manifold before. There was one for sale on Ebay a while back.<P>Sounds like a killer setup!<P>Ryan falconer is still around and on the net. He is well known for building hi Hp 60 degree motors. May want to pick his brain on a few things. I believe he concentrates on V-12's now.<P>JM||||reg||1
